# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Without this, `docker build` sends the whole working tree to the
# daemon — including `src-tauri/target/`, which is gigabytes of Rust
# build output that the image never uses. The first build of the CI
# image transferred 150 MB+ of context before it even started.
#
# The image builds the app itself, so the build output and the
# dependencies are deliberately excluded.

# Build output
target/
src-tauri/target/
dist/
node_modules/

# Local state that must never enter an image
.git/
.gitignore
.internal-identifiers.local
internal-identifiers.txt
*.bundle
*.env
.env.local

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
Thumbs.db

# Python bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# macOS junk
*.dmg.tmp
